%description:

Tcp.fastopenServerEnabled:on-ipv6 -- over IPv6, the server gives a cookie and takes the data of the next SYN with it.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, server: give cookies and accept data on a SYN with
a valid cookie (RFC 7413)".

The class on-ipv6: the cookie of the server is a MAC over the address of the client
(Tcp.cc, appendAddressBytes()), which takes the 16 bytes of an IPv6 address. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test
separates "on" from "off" over IPv6, where the server gives no cookie.

Host under test: host2, on IPv6 nodes (precondition). host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open
at 3.1 s, and connection 2 at 3.5 s with 500 bytes. Observation: level 1, the SYN-ACK of
connection 1 carries a cookie of 8 bytes, and the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges the 500
bytes of its SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenServerEnabled
%# class: on-ipv6
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenServerEnabledOnIpv6")
        .act(action().at(3.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 1: a cookie of 8 bytes")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(3.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2, with 500 bytes")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 501")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges the SYN and the 500 bytes")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenServerEnabledOnIpv6 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host*.typename = "StandardHost6"
*.configurator.typename = "Ipv6FlatNetworkConfigurator"
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenServerEnabledOnIpv6: PASS
